# the Mach-O reader, bytes into the Mach-O model
#
# both widths and both byte orders read through the shared parse shell, and a
# fat file reads into its own model, a header and the bytes of each slice. the
# reader walks exactly ncmds load commands inside sizeofcmds, types the fixed
# fields of each by its cmd and holds the rest of the command as it was, then
# lays out the file after the commands as extents: section bytes, section
# relocations and the data one field pair of a load command names, with raw
# extents over every byte no record covers, so a writer gives back every input
# byte. the symbol, string, table of contents, module, reference, indirect
# symbol, hint and relocation tables are decoded here, and so is every link-edit
# blob and unwind section a codec decodes: the rebase, bind, lazy bind and weak
# bind streams, the export trie, chained fixups, function starts, data in code,
# the code signature, the unwind info and the compact unwind. a decoded blob is
# held as its entries only when encoding them gives its bytes back, and as raw
# bytes with the reason otherwise. a codec that finds the content malformed,
# truncated or overflowing refuses the file. every declared count, offset and
# size is untrusted.

